          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has focal epilepsy of structural etiology, with onset at 8 years of age. Seizures are focal to bilateral tonic-clonic and currently occur approximately twice per month. The epilepsy is drug responsive.\n\nCurrent Medication:\n- Valproate\n\nSeizure Burden:\nApproximately 2 focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures per month.\n\nAssessment:\nDrug-responsive focal epilepsy with focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures. MRI demonstrates a vascular malformation, consistent with the documented structural etiology.\n\nPlan:\n- Continue valproate.\n- Continue monitoring seizure frequency and clinical response.\n\nSincerely,\nEpilepsy Clinic",
